; two interpreters of word streams (the stream's word an index, 0 ends it):
; records of 4 bytes, a 16-bit offset from the table's second record and a
; number added to the stream's position; no bound check, the counts are up
; to the code after the table (its first offset)
rwords     CODE:2D18F 20 stride=4 from=2D193 ; LEA at CODE:2CF36 and CODE:2D148, call through CODE:2CF57 and CODE:2D169; record 0 leads to a RET
rwords     CODE:2F625 1A stride=4 from=2F625 ; LEA at CODE:2F4A4 and CODE:2F5A2, call through CODE:2F4C5 and CODE:2F5C4; record 0 at CODE:2F621 is 0,0 (index 0 not called)
; the event language (2026-09-29, read from the handlers; the operand kinds
; checked on the four modules with tools/event_streams.py: every stream it
; finds parses to its end with relocated pointers, none in both languages).
; A position is a byte offset from the stream's first command.
comment    CODE:2D080 the event queue's runner: the stream at state+2A22h, else the next of the ring at [state+2A1Eh] (index state+2A1Ch, filled by EVENT_QUEUE); one command a call, by the table at CODE:2D18F (record n at +4n: the handler's offset from CODE:2D193 and the command's size, added to the stream's position word +2 before the call); commands from +4, opcode 0 ends the stream
comment    CODE:2CD3C the mode stream (state+0D5Eh, from event opcode 9), one command a call from CODE:2CEF1; while opcode 1Ch waits (state+0D50h) its timer state+0D62h counts down (whole seconds to state+2A6Eh, 2A6Fh) and the stream goes on at its next command once the record at state+0D66h is no longer lit for the player, or at the position state+0D6Ah when the time is up (CODE:2CE98); while it waits and opcode 1Bh's multiball (state+0D2Eh) is down to one ball (state+0D51h), at the position state+0D6Ch (opcode 1Eh; 0: state+0D6Ah)
comment    CODE:2D36E event opcode 1 (a slot-15 record): lit for the current player (its bit, CODE:0038, in byte +1) unless lit already or blocked (byte +2); newly lit: its lamp (the light state at +4) on unless a mode runs and flag bit 4 (byte +0) is set, its +0Ch through CODE:3007A, its display stream +14h through CODE:2FEDB; then no timer (+2Eh = -1) and the record on the list at state+2A32h (once: bit 2 of byte +0)
comment    CODE:2D491 event opcode 2 (a slot-15 record, a word): as opcode 1, lit for a time: nothing when blocked, the lamp, +0Ch and +14h each time; +2Eh = the word times FRAME_RATE (state+50h), counted down on the list by LIT_LIST_STEP
comment    CODE:2D67E event opcode 3 (a slot-15 record): blocked for the current player (byte +2): its lamp off (CODE:2E82F), unlit when its timer runs and flag bit 1 is clear, the timer stopped (+2Eh = -1)
comment    CODE:2D23E event opcode 4 (an object, a word): when the object's word +0 is 1, its byte +0Bh cleared and the word (0, 1 or FFFFh in the modules) to CODE:28E5D, into the table at CODE:288DC by the object's number at +44h (1..0Ah in the modules); DROPS_DRAW draws it on a change: the object is a drop target, the word its state (0 up, else down)
comment    CODE:2D907 event opcode 5 (a slot-15 record): taken (CODE:2D916) when lit for the current player and not blocked: unlit, its points (CODE:2FBBF: packed BCD, the word +24h and dword +28h, e.g. 05000000h, to the player's +10h, the bonus presumably; +1Ch/+20h to its +8), lit again when flag bit 1 or 3 is set, else its lamp off; its display stream +18h through CODE:2FEDB, the player's bit in byte +5 of the light state at +8, its +10h through CODE:3007A, then its handler by the word +2Ch (CODE:2D9DE)
comment    CODE:2D827 event opcode 6 (a slot-16 counter): its dwords +28h, +2Ch to +30h, +34h
comment    CODE:2D8A6 event opcode 7 (a slot-16 counter, two dwords): the dwords to the counter's +30h, +34h
comment    CODE:2D785 event opcode 8 (a hole: the object of a type-4 zone): bit 1 cleared, +34h 0, pushed on the stack at state+2A64h (down from FA48h); CODE:30BD6 takes them one at a time, CODE:30CFB puts the ball the hole holds (byte +1) out at the hole's +6, +8 with the speed +0Ah, +0Ch on the level +0Eh: an eject
comment    CODE:2DA7B event opcode 9 (an event stream): unless state+0D4Fh is set, the stream becomes the running mode stream (state+0D5Eh, state+0D4Fh FFh, the wait and loop state cleared) and the records on the list at state+2A32h with flag bit 4 get their lamps off for the player; in the modules the stream with the mode's opcode 13h (its CD track) is started only this way
comment    CODE:2D5F4 event opcode 0Ah (a position): the stream's position: a jump
comment    CODE:2D210 event opcode 0Bh (a word): state+0D3Eh = the word times FRAME_RATE (state+50h), counted down a frame at CODE:2B86B; while it runs a lost ball is served again (before CODE:2C1A5, and CODE:2B946) and the lamp at header slot 25's second pointer blinks (CODE:2B883): a ball save, presumably
comment    CODE:2DB8E event opcode 0Ch (a slot-15 record): unblocked for the current player (byte +2)
comment    CODE:2D274 event opcode 0Dh (a slot-16 counter): reset: +30h, +34h from +28h, +2Ch, the current player's words +6 and +16h to the word +2, +38h and +3Ch 0; each threshold (12 bytes from +50h, to a negative one) gets the player's bit in byte +2 cleared and its lamp (+8) off
comment    CODE:2D326 event opcode 0Eh (a slot-15 record): unless flag bit 1 is set, unlit for the current player and its lamp off
comment    CODE:2DB5C event opcode 0Fh (a slot-26 BCD counter): started: its start value (+0Ah, +0Eh) to the current one (+2, +6), byte +0 FFh; moved by CODE:2EACF (docs/bpc-module.md, slot 26)
comment    CODE:2DB7B event opcode 10h (a slot-26 BCD counter): stopped (byte +0 cleared)
comment    CODE:2D6F9 event opcode 11h (a display stream): to CODE:2FEDB, the display queue
comment    CODE:2D843 event opcode 12h (a slot-16 counter, two dwords): the dwords to +38h, +3Ch
comment    CODE:2D5E0 event opcode 13h (an audio record): to MUSIC_REQUEST (run, table 1: record 1, track 0)
comment    CODE:2DBAD event opcode 14h (an object of the module): to state+2A70h, the host vector to [CODE:0010], the object's dword +0 called (PUSH, RET); CODE:2CFC8 calls its +4 later (docs/bpc-module.md, "Deferred event dispatch"; table 2's is the music chooser, "Table 2's music chooser" there)
comment    CODE:2CFC8 when no event stream runs and the queue's next entry is empty (further tests of state+2A2Eh and +2A28h not followed): the module object's +4 (state+2A70h) called with the host vector in [CODE:0010]; its return with ZF clear ends it (state+2A70h and 2A74h cleared, state+2A7Fh FFh), with ZF set it is called again
comment    CODE:2D85F event opcode 15h (a slot-16 counter, a word): the current player's words +6 and +16h = the word
comment    CODE:2D7F9 event opcode 16h (a slot-16 counter): the current player's words +6 and +16h = the counter's word +2
comment    CODE:2D8C2 event opcode 17h (a slot-15 record, a position): unless the record is lit for the current player and not blocked (bytes +1, +2), a jump to the position: past the take that follows, in table 1's stream 4F50h
comment    CODE:2D7BE event opcode 18h (a hole, a second hole): as opcode 8, with bit 1 set and the second hole in +34h, whose +6..+0Eh CODE:30CEC takes instead: the ball comes out at the second hole (table 1's modes: held in 4F18h, out at 4DB0h)
comment    CODE:2D358 event opcode 19h: when state+0E44h (RES_CODE, 0..3) is 5, a call of CODE:B927, a RET: no effect (in the modules as often as opcode 1Bh)
comment    CODE:2D60A event opcode 1Ah (a hole): its ball (byte +1 less one, an index into state+C107Ah) let go (bit 1 and byte +1 cleared, +34h 0) and put at 11Ch, 1FEh (CODE:29A5A; the plunger lane, presumably); balls on the table (state+0D32h) one less, to be served (state+0D3Ah) one more
comment    CODE:2D70E event opcode 1Bh (a word, at most 0Dh): balls to be served (state+0D3Ah) added until they and those on the table (state+0D32h) are the word; state+0D2Eh FFh, watched by CODE:2CD3C: a multiball
comment    CODE:2DBDF event opcode 1Ch (a slot-15 record or 0, a word, a position): the mode stream waits (state+0D50h, see CODE:2CD3C): the record, when lit, to state+0D66h; the word times FRAME_RATE (state+50h) to state+0D62h (0: on at once to the position; negative: no timer); the position to state+0D6Ah
comment    CODE:2D6CC event opcode 1Dh (a position): while the count at state+0D6Eh is not 0, it is counted down and the stream goes to the position: a loop
comment    CODE:2D88D event opcode 1Eh (a position): to state+0D6Ch, where a waiting mode stream goes once the multiball is down to one ball
comment    CODE:2D5C7 event opcode 1Fh (a word): the loop count state+0D6Eh (opcode 1Dh)
; the lit records' timers and the lamps (2026-09-29, read from the code and
; the four modules' header slot 14; no run made for it). A light state
; (docs/bpc-module.md, slot 14) as these routines use it: byte +0 and
; byte +5 a bit a player (on), +1 FFh or 0 (the blink phase; 0: dark),
; +2 bit 1 blinking, bit 2 not drawn, +3 the blink count, +4 its reload
name       CODE:2E8CD LIT_LIST_STEP ; the list of lit slot-15 records, a frame
comment    CODE:2E8CD once a frame (CODE:2B4B9 in play, and the loop at CODE:2BB5C) along the slot-15 records on the list at state+2A32h (last state+2A36h, next +30h; flag bit 2 while on it), for the current player (state+0D72h, its bit state+0D74h): a record not lit for the player (byte +1), or whose timer +2Eh is 0, is unlit, its lamp off (LAMP_OFF), +2Eh 0, flag bit 2 cleared, and it leaves the list; a timer above 0 is counted down one, and while it is then at most FRAME_RATE (the last game second) the lamp is put off each frame; otherwise, and with no timer (+2Eh negative), the lamp is put on blinking each frame (the player's bit in its byte +0, byte +2 bit 1, +4 = 8) unless the record is blocked for the player (byte +2); neither while a mode runs (state+0D5Eh) and flag bit 4 is set. So opcode 2 with n seconds: the lamp blinks for n-1 game seconds, is dark for the last, and the record is unlit n x FRAME_RATE + 1 frames after (run 2026-09-29, table 1: the skill shot's record 43D2h lit for 5 s at t=138.267, +2Eh 131h (305), 7 less every 0.1 s, the lamp's byte +1 FFh/00h in turn, bytes +0 and +2 cleared from +2Eh 3Ch on, unlit by CODE:2E952 at t=142.614)
name       CODE:2E82F LAMP_OFF      ; the lamp of the slot-15 record [CODE:0008] off for the player
comment    CODE:2E82F the light state at +4 of the record at [CODE:0008], for the player CODE:0038: its bit in byte +0 cleared, byte +2 bits 0 and 1 cleared (not blinking), +1 FFh, +3 and +4 0
name       CODE:2EF7A LIGHTS_STEP   ; the light states of header slot 14's groups, a frame
comment    CODE:2EF7A once a frame (CODE:2B49A) along the groups of header slot 14 (state+28DEh; the place state+16AEh, the light's number state+16ACh), starting groups until 20h lights are visited in the call, and at most 8 lights drawn in it (a group cut off by that is visited again from its start in the next call): a blinking light (+2 bit 1) counts +3 down and below 0 inverts +1 and reloads +3 from +4, so the blink is counted in visits, not frames; a light is shown when +1 is not 0 and its byte +0 or +5 has the current player's bit (state+0D72h), drawn on (CODE:28FBA) or off (CODE:28FF8) when that differs from state+16B2h+number, and not drawn with +2 bit 2. A group whose lights were all shown and none blinking gets, unless its byte +4 has bit 1 (the groups with no stream in the modules), bit 0 set, once: its event stream +6 to EVENT_QUEUE and CODE:2EF17 (a word 10h and the group to the list at state+1822h, bit 0 of each light's byte +2 set; not followed). Then, once a press of a flipper key (state+2A7Bh, 2A7Ch; the latch state+2A7Ah), each group of the zero-ended list stored backwards before header slot 14's first pointer gets its lights' bytes +0 turned one place: each light takes the next one's, the last the first's (the lane change, presumably). That list holds one group in tables 2, 3 and 4 (96E4h and 8FD6h with 3 lights, 91B0h with 4), none in table 1
; the drop targets (2026-09-29, read from the code and the four modules'
; objects; no run made for it). An object of type 1 (word +0) of the
; 0C0h dwords at header slot 4 (state+28B6h, zeros between): its number
; +44h, down +0Bh (FFh), a light state +2, its sound record +6, its bank
; +22h, the next of its bank +1Eh, the picture's place +2Eh, +32h, its
; picture pair +36h, a width +42h (0: the picture's), the mask +3Ah at
; the byte +26h, bit shift +3Eh, of the level +2Ah picks (1: header slot
; 1's map, else slot 7's). A bank: the first target +0, no raising
; with bit 0 of +4, points before +16h (12 BCD digits), an event stream
; +16h. Found this way: table 1 one bank of 2 (5128h), table 4 three
; (3, 3, 2 targets: 472Ch, 49AAh, 4AA2h; 472Ch with bit 0), tables 2
; and 3 none
name       CODE:28E5D DROP_SET      ; the state [CODE:0020] of the drop target [CODE:0000] into the table CODE:288DC (8 bytes by its number: the state, the state drawn, the object)
name       CODE:28EA6 DROPS_DRAW    ; each frame (CODE:298C5, after BALLS_STEP) the 64h entries of CODE:288DC
comment    CODE:28EA6 an entry whose state differs from the one drawn: the picture +36h x 2, less 1 when the state is odd (from drops.mgl, the "Droptargets (Gfx)" load at CODE:28D64), drawn at +2Eh, +32h (CODE:290D7), and its mask put into the level's map (DROP_MASK)
name       CODE:2942C DROP_MASK     ; the drop target's mask (masks.mgl) cleared from the level's map (a state not 0) or set in it (0); the map a bit a pixel, 2Ah bytes (336 pixels) a line; four routines by the width 10h, 18h, 20h, 30h; the ball's collisions with the map, presumably, not followed
name       CODE:2C7FC OBJECT_HITS   ; each frame (CODE:2B4B9) for each ball in play (byte +9 0): its word +6Ch (not negative) picks an object in the table at its +60h (header slot 4 or 10, by the level: CODE:2C414, 2C467), handled by the object's type (word +0, switch at CODE:2C8BC: 0 CODE:2C8C2, 1 DROP_HIT, 2 CODE:2CB03; types 0 and 2 not followed); who sets +6Ch not followed
name       CODE:2C9D4 DROP_HIT      ; a drop target hit by a ball
comment    CODE:2C9D4 the player's bit (state+0D72h) set in byte +0 of the light state +2, the bank's points (+0Eh..+15h, TAKE_PAY), the record +6 to CODE:9F2C (as a record of type 2 through RECORD_DISPATCH), down (+0Bh FFh) and queued for DROP_SET (state+2A60h); when every target of the bank is down: the bank's stream +16h to EVENT_QUEUE, and unless its +4 bit 0 is set the bank onto the stack state+2AD0h to be raised (DROPS_RAISE_STEP). Run 2026-09-29, table 1, blind play: target 5188h hit at t=205.128 and again one frame later, 5142h at 209.887 and 209.901; the bank's stream (5128h +16h: light 51E0h, block 5218h) queued at both of the last two, 51E0h lit; so a hit is handled in two frames running, presumably while the ball's +6Ch stays
name       CODE:30799 DROPS_RAISE_STEP ; each frame (CODE:30784 from CODE:2B49A): with no bank waiting, one taken from the stack state+2AD0h and 64h frames set (state+2AD8h); when they run out every target of the bank is up (+0Bh 0) and queued for DROP_SET
name       CODE:3086D DROPS_QUEUE_STEP ; each frame: one entry of the queue at state+2A60h (a word, 1: a drop target, whose +0Bh goes to DROP_SET)
name       CODE:2A39A DROPS_UP_ALL  ; at the game start (GAME_PHASE 2, CODE:2A976): every drop target up (DROP_SET at once), the stacks at state+2AD0h, 2A60h and 2A64h (the holes') set empty
name       CODE:2A421 DROPS_UP_BALL ; at the next ball (CODE:2BCC0): every drop target up but those with bit 0 of +4
; the holes' eject (2026-09-29, read from the code; no run made for it).
; A hole (the object of a type-4 zone): bit 1 of +0 set by opcode 18h
; (the ball out at the second hole, +34h), byte +1 the ball held (its
; number + 1 in state+C107Ah's table), the count +4, where the ball comes
; out +6, +8, its speed +0Ah, +0Ch, the level +0Eh (0 or 1), a sound
; record +10h, an object of the table CODE:285BC +30h (drawn by CODE:28E7B)
name       CODE:30996 HOLE_EJECT_STEP ; each frame (CODE:30784 from CODE:2B49A): the hole ejecting (state+2A68h), else the next from the stack state+2A64h
comment    CODE:30996 with bit 1 the second hole (+34h) stands in for the hole in what follows but the count. A count below 0 counts up and at 0 puts the ball out at once (CODE:30C5C). A count above 0 counts down: at 3Ch the ball is put out (CODE:30CAD), below 32h every 8th frame the sound record +10h (CODE:9F2C) and each frame the object +30h drawn in state count AND 4 (CODE:28E7B: it flickers every 4 frames), at 0 the hole is done (state+2A68h 0; without bit 1 the program's own record CODE:100E8, a sound presumably, through RECORD_DISPATCH), its ball no longer held (bit 7 of the ball's byte +1). Without bit 1 the sound record is read from [CODE:0004]+10h, and CODE:0004 then still holds what DROPS_QUEUE_STEP left there (state+2A60h's place), not the hole: a slip, as read; what sounds there not checked
comment    CODE:30BD6 the next hole from the stack state+2A64h (opcode 8, 18h): its count +4 is 4Ch (76 frames) when the hole that puts the ball out has an object at +30h, else FFCEh (-50: 50 frames, no picture). Run 2026-09-29, table 1: 4Ch twice (t=148.980, 171.732), the ball out 0.223 and 0.227 s later (16 frames); FFCEh not seen
comment    CODE:30CFB the ball out: its words +12h, +14h = +6, +8 (and shifted by 0Ah into its dwords +1Eh, +22h), the high bytes of its words +0Eh, +10h cleared and +0Ah, +0Ch added, then onto level +0Eh as zone type 3 (0: CODE:2C414) or type 2 (1: CODE:2C467) do
; the display language (the same way; opcodes 4, 5, 0Bh, 11h, 12h, 15h..17h
; are in none of the modules' streams the tool finds)
comment    CODE:2F35C the display queue's runner: waits while state+2A40h (frames) counts down, and after opcode 7 (state+2A3Ch) while an animation of opcode 1 runs (state+2A50h), then while state+2A3Eh counts down; else one command of the running stream (state+2A2Eh, else the next of the ring at [state+2A2Ah], filled by CODE:2FEDB) by the table at CODE:2F621 (record n at +4n, as CODE:2D18F; commands from +6, the position word at +4); with none queued, the background stream (state+2A58h) runs to its end at once (CODE:2F555)
comment    CODE:2FEDB a display stream to the queue: word +0 bit 0 set: it becomes the background stream (state+2A58h); else by its bytes +2, +3 against the running one's (state+2A3Ah, 2A3Bh): +2 lower, or equal and +3 lower, dropped; +2 higher or negative, or both equal: the queue emptied, the displays cleared (CODE:2FBA8, BA9B) and it queued; +2 equal and +3 higher: queued behind
comment    CODE:2F9CF display opcode 1 (an animation, five words): state+2A50h = it (a wait of opcode 7 waits for it first); its +6..+0Eh from the words (the first shifted right by 4 and doubled), +12h from +22h, +10h and +16h cleared; played by ANIMS_STEP; state+2A50h also cleared when DISPLAY_QUEUE empties the queue (CODE:2FF7A)
comment    CODE:2F7A5 display opcode 2: both display buffers cleared (CODE:2FBA8)
comment    CODE:2FB17 display opcode 3 (a text record): through CODE:27783 (host vector +14h, docs/bpc-module.md)
comment    CODE:2FBA4 display opcodes 4, 15h, 16h, 17h (a dword each): a RET
comment    CODE:2FB2C display opcode 5 (a pointer, four words): the word before the pointer, its bytes swapped, AND 0FFFh, shown as a number (CODE:1010A), the words its layout (CODE:002C..0038)
comment    CODE:2F712 display opcode 6 (a pointer, four words): the packed-BCD number that ends at the pointer shown through CODE:275E4 (host vector +10h), the words its layout (CODE:002C..0038)
comment    CODE:2FB6F display opcode 7 (a word): waits the word times FRAME_RATE (state+50h) in frames (state+2A3Eh, 2A3Ch)
comment    CODE:2FA88 display opcode 8 (four words): the current player's score (the record at state+0D76h, its +8) shown through CODE:275E4; the third word 1 becomes 3 when the record's word +0 is not 0 (not followed)
comment    CODE:2F812 display opcode 9 (a pointer, four words): the current player's word (at the pointer plus twice the player, less 2), AND 0FFFh, shown as a number (CODE:1015E)
comment    CODE:2F7B1 display opcode 0Ah (a word): waits that many frames (state+2A40h)
comment    CODE:2F7CA display opcode 0Bh (a code address): called, with [CODE:0000] = it
comment    CODE:2F68D display opcode 0Ch (an animation, five words, the fifth not read): as opcode 1 into state+2A5Ch, without the wait; nothing when it is the one there already
; the animations (2026-09-29, read from the code and the four modules'
; display streams; no run made for it). An animation record of the
; module: +0 the next played beside it (0 in every record opcodes 1 and
; 0Ch name), +6 the place ((word >> 4) x 2, times 4 the byte offset in
; the buffer), +0Eh repeats (the fifth word: 0 in most uses, up to 9),
; +10h/+11h a step every +11h+1 calls (1..3 in the modules), +12h the
; frames left, +16h the frame's data, +1Ah, +1Eh its width and height,
; +22h the frame count, +24h the first frame's number in
; data\s00n\anims\allanims.mgl ("Manglade Anims", CODE:2791F)
name       CODE:27A0E ANIMS_STEP    ; a step of the display's animations, a call a frame after DISPLAY_RUN (CODE:2A690, 2B83D, 2B95A, 2BA0A)
comment    CODE:27A0E the list at state+2A50h (opcode 1; last state+2A54h), each record a step: the next frame drawn (ANIM_FRAME), and after +22h of them it starts again while +0Eh counts down, else it leaves the list (its +0 cleared; the list's head then 0: DISPLAY_RUN's wait of opcode 7 ends). A record still counting +10h ends the call. With the list empty, the animation of opcode 0Ch (state+2A5Ch) plays the same way but starts again for ever; it is set back to its first frame while the list plays or a display stream runs (state+2A2Eh), and then not drawn
name       CODE:27C2A ANIM_FRAME    ; one frame into the 160-byte-a-line buffer (1400h bytes, 160 x 32, cleared to FCh by CODE:27CEC; the dot display, presumably)
comment    CODE:27C2A a new start (+16h 0) takes frame +24h (1 when not below the file's count, its dword 0), its header words width, height, count to +1Ah, +1Eh, +22h (and +12h); a data byte up to 4 is a pixel of colour FCh + byte (4: 00h), above 4 skips byte - 4 pixels; the frames follow one another in the file (+16h goes on past the one drawn)
comment    CODE:2F7AB display opcode 0Dh: one display buffer cleared (CODE:27259)
comment    CODE:2F982 display opcode 0Eh (four words): as opcode 5 with the word at state+2A6Eh: the seconds left of the mode stream's wait (CODE:2CD3C)
comment    CODE:2F79F display opcode 0Fh: the other display buffer cleared (CODE:27CEC)
comment    CODE:2FB02 display opcode 10h (a record): through CODE:3007A (by its type: an audio record, a slot-31 record, ...)
comment    CODE:2FA55 display opcode 11h: a RET
comment    CODE:2F755 display opcode 12h (four words): as opcode 8 with the player record's +10h
comment    CODE:2FAE9 display opcode 13h (a word): the loop count state+2A4Eh (opcode 14h)
comment    CODE:2FA56 display opcode 14h (a position): state+2A4Eh counted down; unless it is 0, a jump to the position: a loop
comment    CODE:2F80C display opcode 18h: DAC colours FCh..FFh from the second set (CODE:BAB6)
comment    CODE:2F9C9 display opcode 19h: DAC colours FCh..FFh from the first set (CODE:BA9B)
comment    CODE:2F7DE display opcode 1Ah (a text record, a word): shown (CODE:27783) when the word AND the word at CODE:BAD4 is not 0; CODE:BAD4 is counted up by DRV_TICK (CODE:B99C, the sound driver's command-0Eh routine; how often not checked): blinking text
; the zones' types (the switch at CODE:2C3DD; the object at the zone's +0Ah)
comment    CODE:2C59C zone type 0: as type 1 (from CODE:2C61F), first, when state+0D2Fh is set, the event stream of header slot 27 (state+2912h) or 28 (2916h) to EVENT_QUEUE by whether state+0E38h equals state+0D36h (not followed): a skill shot, presumably
comment    CODE:2C4B5 zone type 1: on entry the object's points (from +1Eh; through CODE:2FD11 from +26h instead when the record at +0Ah has the player's bit already), its +2 through CODE:3007A, its +6 (an event stream) to EVENT_QUEUE
comment    CODE:2C462 zone type 2: the ball's +50h..+64h from header slots 6..11 (state+28BEh), byte +8 FFh: onto the other level, presumably
comment    CODE:2C40F zone type 3: the ball's +50h..+64h from header slots 0..5 (state+28A6h), byte +8 0
comment    CODE:2C719 zone type 4, a hole: unless the ball is held (bit 7 of its byte +1), when the hole's byte +1 is 0 it holds the ball (its number to byte +1), the points before +2Ch (CODE:2FBBF), the main program's record at CODE:100CE through CODE:3007A, the event stream at +14h to EVENT_QUEUE
words      CODE:2DA0A 1C CODE      ; PUSH [EBX*4+2DA0A] at CODE:2DA02 after PUSH 2DA09h, then RET: by the word at [[CODE:0008]+2Ch] (0 not taken); 28 up to the first target (a RET at CODE:2DA7A)
words      CODE:2CD10 0B CODE      ; its address put in [CODE:0010] (CODE:2BEDC, 2D04D, 2DBD3) before calls into the table module: its host vector (docs/bpc-module.md), +14h (CODE:27783) draws a text record, +1Ch is EVENT_QUEUE (checked 2026-09-29: table 1's and 2's arguments there are event streams), the others not checked one by one

; the keyboard (runs of 2026-09-29 with doskit's -rwatch on CODE:D984)
code       CODE:A076 KBD_IRQ       ; installed at CODE:A03B with INT 93h AH=4 BL=1 (presumably IRQ1's vector; the old one saved with AH=3); run: entered on each key event, CS=000C
ds         CODE:A08E-A10B CODE     ; DS from CODE:A10B (the selector made at CODE:A323 from DS); run: its writes land at CODE's addresses (KEY_DOWN below)
name       CODE:D984 KEY_DOWN     ; 256 bytes, FFh while the key is down: the scan code, +80h after an E0h prefix (run: +2Ah FFh on Left Shift down, 00h on its release)
name       CODE:DA84 KEY_TOGGLE    ; the same index, the byte inverted on each press
name       CODE:A016 LAST_KEY      ; the last scan code pressed (without 80h); also stored at CODE:CC2F
name       CODE:A01D KEY_E0        ; FFh after an E0h prefix
name       CODE:A2C7 KEY_RELEASED  ; FFh after a release: a press of Space (39h) or Alt (38h, E0 38h) counts only then (no typematic repeat for them, presumably)
; reads of KEY_DOWN through the record at [CODE:0014] (CB3Eh in the runs:
; KEY_DOWN is its field E46h); the field offsets stay numbers
comment    CODE:144BA Space (KEY_DOWN+39h) pushes the word at [ESI+0D48h] up by 258h a frame to 3E8h, then clears the key; down by C8h without it: presumably a nudge (upward), not checked
num        CODE:144BA
num        CODE:14520
comment    CODE:145A0 Left Alt (KEY_DOWN+38h) and Right Alt (+B8h) move the word at [ESI+0D46h] down / up by 258h to -3E8h / 3E8h: presumably nudges left and right, not checked; Space, Left Alt, Right Alt set bits 0, 1, 2 of [ESI+2A77h] on a new press
num        CODE:145A0
num        CODE:1460A
num        CODE:1461C
num        CODE:14686
comment    CODE:14757 the flippers (run: Left Shift held, the left flipper up in the picture): left = Left Shift or Left Ctrl (KEY_DOWN+2Ah, +1Dh) to [ESI+2A7Bh], right = Right Shift or Right Ctrl (+36h, E0 1Dh) to [ESI+2A7Ch]
num        CODE:14757
num        CODE:1475D
num        CODE:14769
num        CODE:1476F
comment    CODE:2F300 Enter (KEY_DOWN+1Ch) launches the waiting ball (run: F1, then Enter: the ball moves; Down, held 3 s, is read by no one): the index at [[ESI+2906h]] cleared, 1770h taken from the word +10h of the object at [ESI+1076h+index*4] (presumably its speed, upward)
num        CODE:2F306
num        CODE:2F315
comment    CODE:2A7FD in the attract mode: Esc (KEY_DOWN+1) to CODE:2A8AB; F1..F8 (+3Bh..+42h, the field at [ESI+0E81h]) or keypad Enter (E0 1Ch) set [ESI+8Eh] to 2 and add the key's number (1..8; keypad Enter 1) to [ESI+0D70h] (run: F1 starts a game, "PLAYERS 1"; the others not tried)

; offsets among the 32-bit immediates (2026-09-29): ptrscan.py (49) and a
; throwaway scan of every 4-byte immediate from 100h to the image's end that
; was no label (642 besides branches), each sorted by how its register is
; used next and by eye. Numbers left as they are: counts in ECX, sizes in
; EBX for INT 92h, strides (C4E0h, 1500h, 5C0h), offsets in other selectors
; (video memory after OUT 3C4h; ES/DS/FS from INT 93h AH=5, CODE:130F, A117,
; 634A/634C, 3B4B) and a CD time (CODE:35DE8). ES from CODE:A10B, 131D, 635E
; is taken for CODE (copies of DS, presumably the start-up alias). Lengths of
; checksummed stretches (ECX before CODE:4CE8/4CF2/7438/7441) stay numbers:
; the kit has no label differences.
comment    CODE:523B the dword at 290FBh+7CBh = CODE:298C6 is the immediate of MOV EBX,14DE2h; CALL EBX at CODE:298C5: overwritten here with [[CODE:5DCB]+13h]+[CODE:55E3] (the variable the dead copy-protection pieces write) when the byte at CODE:037C is 1. CODE:037C is the 0 before the text CODE:0372 prints and no instruction in the image names it but the CMP here; runs of 2026-09-29 (the chooser left for table 1 and by Esc): CODE:523B not reached, CODE:298C6 written once, by the loader at t=2.28, and CODE:298C5 called 14DE2h once a frame. Presumably the protection's switch, dead in this release as its pieces are; the base 290FBh left a number
comment    CODE:4FF9 the chooser (reached at t=97.6 in the runs); it ends at CODE:51D6 when a table is chosen (t=106.56, the CD stop there) or on Esc (t=101.11, the program then exits with 32): the sound driver's commands 5 and 0Bh, the selector in CODE:8138 freed, CD_STOP, a checksummed call
comment    CODE:50A9 a keyboard table by INT 93h AH=15h (a country code in AH:AL, presumably the keyboard's; not checked): BE and FR the AZERTY one at CODE:6023, the eight codes at CODE:50EE (HU, YU, SF, SG, CZ, SL, PL, GR) the QWERTZ one at CODE:5F22, else the QWERTY one at CODE:5E21 (the runs); copied upper-case to CODE:2B0A2, FFh for what is not a character
comment    CODE:29889 the frame step (runs: CODE:298C5 about 70 times a second on table 1): the four routines of the table at [CODE:2982E], a wait for CODE:BAD1 = FFh (set by the driver's command-0Fh routine CODE:B9B9), then 14DE2h, CODE:28EA6, 14C46, 156C4
comment    CODE:14DE2 each ball on the table (state+0D32h of them, the list at state+1046h) to CODE:0010, then CODE:14DD6 (CODE:26977, 269B0)
comment    CODE:4532 [CODE:3B58] is read with DS from CODE:3B4B (a block freed with INT 92h AH=5, where it is set not found): 430Ah here and 46AFh at CODE:4886 (the text "The GREETINGS Page" in CODE) left numbers until that selector is known
comment    CODE:33D0 a second handler through INT 93h AH=4 BL=1 (as KBD_IRQ at CODE:A05C): CODE:340A, reached by the ptr below
ds         CODE:3416-3450 CODE     ; DS from CODE:131D, a copy of DS (CODE:4CFB), presumably CODE
comment    CODE:340A a keyboard handler: the scan code (port 60h) into a ring of 16 bytes at CODE:1906 (index CODE:1903), shifted into the dword at CODE:1538; releases (80h and up) skipped; when it is installed not looked at
ds         CODE:4C8C-4C92 CODE     ; DS from CODE:131D, as above
comment    CODE:4C85 the routine handed to the sound driver with command 0Eh at CODE:4CB6: counts the dword at CODE:1548 (presumably a timer tick, not checked)
comment    CODE:4C93 the routine handed with command 0Fh (ECX 1999h) at CODE:4CD1: the CRT start address (3D4h, 0Ch/0Dh) from CODE:1323 while CODE:191A is 1
ds         CODE:9CDC-9CE3 CODE     ; DS from CODE:A10B, as KBD_IRQ
comment    CODE:9CD4 the completion routine handed with command 11h at CODE:9B31: sets CODE:9CE5 to FFh; the driver calls it from its command 6 once a jingle has ended (a jump to the order it plays, SB16.SDR +1EAF; run 2026-09-29: 1.69 s after the command 0Ah of order 0Eh)
name       CODE:B99C DRV_TICK      ; handed with command 0Eh at CODE:9B93: counts CODE:BAD4 (the blinking of display opcode 1Ah, the random awards of handler 1Ah)
ds         CODE:B9AA-B9B7 CODE     ; DS from CODE:A10B
comment    CODE:B9B9 handed with command 0Fh at CODE:9BAF (ECX from CODE:9B8E: DDDDh, E898h, EEEEh or F258h, set at CODE:9725..9882): sets CODE:BAD1 to FFh, the CRT start address from CODE:BAD2 (+54h while the word at CODE:D884 is not 0) and, when CODE:00A2 is 3, the attribute controller's pel panning (4 or 6 by the sign of CODE:D884): presumably the screen's scroll per frame, not checked
ds         CODE:B9C3-BA7A CODE     ; DS from CODE:A10B
